{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"slowmotion-stricken-mare","creation_channel":"cli","description":"Operator-approved early removal (pre-1.0 breaking pass #3), 2026-08-12. Source: the DEPRECATION REMOVAL-READINESS SURVEY, comment #11 on childsafe-bizarre-lorikeet (b902-18af-14ed-4da1), Tier 2 item 3. Operator ruling (verbatim): \"The two best candidates and the one ready now are all approved for removal.\" Third and last change of the pass, after checked-unhelpful-tanager and priceless-charred-fruitbat.\n\n## What\n\nRemove the deprecated bare env var `REBAR_LLM_MODEL` (deprecated 1fbfb5c691, shipped v0.11.0; ADR 0057). The per-class `[tool.rebar.llm.model_classes]` slots are the interface; the bare scalar is a SUPERSESSION with a migration window that the operator has now closed early.\n\n## SCOPE NARROWING — the config key `[tool.rebar.llm].model` STAYS\n\nThe survey framed this as \"REBAR_LLM_MODEL / llm.model\". Evidence says only the ENV VAR is removable, and that matches the registry, whose single row (`src/rebar/_deprecations.py:101`) is env-only:\n\n- `rebar.toml` sets `[tool.rebar.llm].model` deliberately and load-bearingly (it pins the provider so provider inference cannot leak to a non-Bedrock default).\n- `LLMConfig.model` is read widely across the runtime and is the value model-class resolution falls back to.\n- `docs/config.md:320` documents `model` as a live key; only its \"env `REBAR_LLM_MODEL`\" annotation goes.\n\nSo this ticket removes ONE env channel and leaves the config key, the CLI `-c llm.model` override, and the per-step `model:` workflow override untouched.\n\n## Scope (current main)\n\n- `src/rebar/_deprecations.py:92-101` — delete the `_scheduled(\"env\", \"REBAR_LLM_MODEL\", …)` row and its explanatory comment block; append this removal to the historical-record NOTE.\n- `src/rebar/_deprecations.py:~249` — ADD the tombstone `_tomb(\"env\", \"REBAR_LLM_MODEL\", \"the [tool.rebar.llm.model_classes] slots\", \"error\")`, directly mirroring the `REBAR_LLM_MAX_ITERS` row at :249.\n- `src/rebar/llm/config.py:529-536` — wire the new tombstone check next to the existing `REBAR_LLM_MAX_ITERS` check in `LLMConfig.from_env`, the same fail-loud placement (a retired LLM knob fails only when the LLM stack loads; `RemovedInputError` is a `BaseException` so the broad `except Exception` in this method cannot swallow it).\n- `src/rebar/llm/config.py:581-597` — delete the warn-when-set block; `:599` — stop reading the env for `model`.\n- `src/rebar/llm/config.py:373` — `_llm_str` gains `env_name: str | None`, skipping the env read when `None`, so `model` resolves CLI > config table > default with no env channel.\n- `src/rebar/llm/model_classes.py:230-250` — delete `_deprecated_bare_model()`; drop the `fallback_default` rung so class precedence becomes CLI > per-class env > config table > built-in default (`:183-189` comment updated).\n\n## Registry/tombstone treatment (mirrors precedent)\n\nDeleted row + historical NOTE is the DE7 / ticket-5899 shape. UNLIKE removal #2, this one DOES take a tombstone: the tombstone registry covers `env`/`cfg`/`file` inputs, and the closest precedent — `_tomb(\"env\", \"REBAR_LLM_MAX_ITERS\", \"REBAR_LLM_MAX_STEPS\", \"error\")`, also a superseded LLM knob checked in `llm.config.from_env` — is `behavior=\"error\"`. Fail-loud is right here because silently ignoring a still-set `REBAR_LLM_MODEL` would quietly change which model every operation runs, i.e. cost and quality, with no signal. Record \"operator-approved early removal (pre-1.0 pass #3), 2026-08-12\".\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The env var is gone from the resolver; checked: `grep -rn REBAR_LLM_MODEL src/rebar` matches only the tombstone row and its check (a raw grep, since env names are string literals the LSP cannot resolve).\n- [ ] A still-set `REBAR_LLM_MODEL` FAILS LOUD with the migration message rather than being ignored; checked: `REBAR_LLM_MODEL=x rebar review-plan --check` exits non-zero naming the model_classes slots.\n- [ ] `[tool.rebar.llm].model`, `-c llm.model` and the per-step `model:` override all still resolve; proven by `pytest tests/unit/test_config_llm.py`.\n- [ ] The deprecation row is deleted and the tombstone added; proven by `pytest tests/unit/test_deprecation_registry.py`.\n- [ ] `docs/env-vars.md` is REGENERATED, not hand-edited, and no longer lists the variable; checked: `python scripts/gen_env_registry.py && git diff --exit-code docs/env-vars.md`.\n- [ ] Hand-written docs drop the variable: `docs/config.md`, `docs/llm-framework.md`, `docs/llm-example-configs.md`, `docs/local-dev-env.md`, `docs/ci-provider-matrix.md`, `docs/plan-review-gate.md`, `docs/workflow-authoring-v2.md`. ADR 0057 stays as historical record.\n- [ ] `docs/release-notes.md` and `CHANGELOG.md` record the removal in the prior passes' table format.\n- [ ] Gates green; checked: `make lint`, `make typecheck`, and the full `pytest` suite.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `make lint` and `make typecheck` — the commit gate.\n- `pytest` (full suite); `tests/unit/test_llm_model_env_deprecation.py` covers the deprecation being removed and is retargeted to the tombstone's fail-loud behaviour.\n- `python scripts/gen_env_registry.py && git diff --exit-code docs/env-vars.md` — the CI env-registry drift gate.\n- `grep -rn REBAR_LLM_MODEL src tests docs` — raw grep for the string-literal env name.","id":"6cc4-56f1-6cc6-4c7f","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Remove the deprecated REBAR_LLM_MODEL env var"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786571503069597001,"uuid":"fae45a9e-505e-4e06-af2a-50c9e66e3429"}